WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.173
Hi, I'm Gudgeon!

00:00:02.173 --> 00:00:05.704
An agent skill makes any card look as if an agent is

00:00:05.704 --> 00:00:07.176
building it, dot by dot.

00:00:07.176 --> 00:00:08.647
No model draws those dots.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:14.290
The idea: measure the real element, draw a dotted wireframe of exactly

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.917
that, then reveal it behind a scan line.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.913
First, it walks the element once.

00:00:22.211 --> 00:00:25.078
Boxes: backgrounds, borders, buttons and images.

00:00:25.498 --> 00:00:28.328
Text lines, from the browser's own line rectangles.

00:00:28.748 --> 00:00:30.487
Small icons, path by path.

00:00:31.013 --> 00:00:33.808
And key elements, which get guides and size labels.

00:00:35.383 --> 00:00:37.567
The element goes in once, and gets measured.

00:00:38.583 --> 00:00:41.113
Out comes a list of parts, each with a start time.

00:00:41.783 --> 00:00:46.083
Every frame, one function takes the build's progress and redraws everything.

00:00:46.503 --> 00:00:48.503
It draws into an overlay on top.

00:00:48.503 --> 00:00:50.502
The real element stays in the page.

00:00:51.942 --> 00:00:53.066
Here is the formula.

00:00:53.942 --> 00:00:57.131
A dash of zero length with a round cap is one dot,

00:00:57.131 --> 00:00:58.460
every four point eight pixels.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:00.024
More dots, more line.

00:01:00.024 --> 00:01:02.027
Slide the offset, and the dots flow.

00:01:03.483 --> 00:01:05.275
A photo is read from its pixels.

00:01:06.072 --> 00:01:07.649
A contour sketch of its tones.

00:01:08.337 --> 00:01:10.558
A halftone, painted once onto a canvas.

00:01:10.978 --> 00:01:12.611
Dots in the photo's own colours.

00:01:13.242 --> 00:01:14.804
Then the photo, out of a blur.

00:01:16.675 --> 00:01:18.681
The cost is the dot field.

00:01:18.681 --> 00:01:22.693
One demo card has seven hundred and eighty-four circles, touched every frame.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.571
The skill picks the variant and the moment.

00:01:27.571 --> 00:01:29.237
The fixed runtime does the drawing.

00:01:33.483 --> 00:01:36.928
To recap: measure first, draw dots with dashes, and keep it

00:01:36.928 --> 00:01:38.181
to one showcase element.

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:40.649
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:40.649 --> 00:01:41.234
I'm Gudgeon.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:41.527
Bye!
